Simulation for Honours Project
This project simulates how different sociopolitical ideologies manage limited energy resources in a shared environment. It extends the Sugarscape agent-based model to include renewable and non-renewable patches, ecological degradation, redistribution systems, environmental policies, and cooperative infrastructure building.

Six ideological agents are implemented: capitalist, green capitalist, socialist, green socialist, communist, and green communist. Each ideology follows its own rule-based decision logic for movement, mining, cooperation, and repair.

The simulation also includes adaptive reinforcement learning agents. One uses a custom Deep Q-Network (DQN) trained inside the Mesa simulation, and the other uses a Stable-Baselines3 DQN trained externally through a Gymnasium wrapper.


